.3 of the mentioned paper</a>).","statement1":"As of 2020-2024, papers containing <span  \"><i>\"wp\" </i></span> tend to be published in lower impact factor journals (<span style=\"color: rgba(105, 219, 99, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">23<sup>rd</sup></span> percentile among all words)  and tend to be cited less (<span style=\"color: rgba(255, 168, 82, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">13<sup>rd</sup></span> percentile word). In general, this word is negatively associated with university ranking, such that higher-ranked institutions are less likely to publish papers containing <span  \"><i>\"wp\" </i></span> (<span style=\"color: rgba(170, 117, 250, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">36<sup>th</sup></span> percentile). "}